# Unison Content OS — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; never commit a key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE SETTING VITE_GROQ_API_KEY
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the built JavaScript. Anyone who can
# open the built page can read the key out of the bundle. That is fine for a
# build that only ever runs on the marketing team's own machines, and wrong
# for a public URL.
#
# Two safer places to put the key, in order of preference:
#
#   1. Settings -> AI inside the app. The key is stored in that browser's
#      localStorage only. It never enters the saved session, an export, or the
#      repository. This is the recommended route and needs nothing here.
#
#   2. GROQ_API_KEY below, with api/ai.js deployed. The key stays on the
#      server and the browser never sees it. Use this for a shared URL.
#
# VITE_GROQ_API_KEY is only a convenience for local development so nobody has
# to paste a key after every hard refresh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Server-side (api/ai.js relay — the key never reaches the browser) ---
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Optional. Only needed if the team wants Anthropic as well.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional shared secret so only your deployment can call the relay.
UNISON_RELAY_TOKEN=
# Optional. Milliseconds before the relay gives up on the model. Default 55000.
AI_TIMEOUT_MS=

# --- Client-side (bundled into the build — see the warning above) ---
# Free key from https://console.groq.com/keys
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=
# "groq" (default, free) or "anthropic" (paid).
VITE_AI_PROVIDER=groq
# Only if the team also uses Anthropic.
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- LinkedIn (optional; api/linkedin.js — see README) ---
# With these set, text and article posts go straight to LinkedIn and Make is
# only needed for image, video, document, poll and carousel posts.
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional. Pin the API version the bridge sends. Defaults to a known-good one.
LINKEDIN_API_VERSION=

# --- Shared team workspace (optional; api/workspace.js — see README) ---
# Without these, every person's posts and calendar stay in their own browser.
# A free Upstash Redis database is enough: https://upstash.com
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# Optional. The key the shared document is stored under.
UNISON_WORKSPACE_KEY=

# ---------- AI artwork and video (optional, paid) ----------
# Set on the SERVER only. The browser never sees these.
# Leave unset and Unison keeps using its own free renderer.
#
# Images — one of:
OPENAI_API_KEY=
#   or
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides:
# OPENAI_IMAGE_MODEL=gpt-image-1
# OPENAI_IMAGE_USD=0.04
# GOOGLE_IMAGE_MODEL=imagen-4.0-generate-001
#
# Video — one of (GOOGLE_API_KEY above also covers Veo):
RUNWAY_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_VIDEO_MODEL=veo-3.1-fast-generate-001
# GOOGLE_VIDEO_USD_SEC=0.05
# RUNWAY_VIDEO_USD_SEC=0.12
